    "body": "Scope addition for U6 (to keep the PR count low). U6 also closes these gaps between the merged U1 to U4 and the mock-up of #3663:\n\n1. Editor layout: the parameters on the left and the preview on the right, as in the mock-up picture 2. U3 (#3914) put the preview above the tabs.\n2. Preview toggles: show or hide the dimension lines and the holder. The flutes toggle comes with #3908 (3D flutes).\n3. List rows: a small drawing of each tool, and a gauge-length column (holder gauge length + stick-out), as in mock-up picture 1.\n4. Categories on the left of the list (end mill, ball mill, drill, chamfer and so on, from the tool kind), as in mock-up picture 1, if U2 (#3903) did not add them.\n\nEach item keeps the existing rules: no new command for display changes, the Frame cost rule for the row drawings (cached, keyed on the tool value), and the window layout tests updated.",
